**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The Library suite becomes a contract suite that any live Library and any preset store run (001 §C 'Contract tests' and 'the `LibraryProxy` live view, and the preset … stores'; .spec-md §9; the S2.3 brief: the preset store's contract lives in `LibraryProxyTests`), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs`: the test-local record `LiveLibraryStores = { library : LibraryProxy; samples : SampleProxy; sources : SourceProxy }` is a live Library with the samples and user-sources stores it composes. `[<AbstractClass>] type LibraryProxyContract ()` declares `abstract liveStores : unit -> LiveLibraryStores`, a live Library over stores holding the Built-in catalogue and no user source, and `abstract emptyPresetStore : unit -> LibraryEntryStore`, a preset store holding nothing. These 10 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `entriesForKind Sample returns only SampleItems`; `entriesForKind Detector returns only DetectorItems`; `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer returns ONLY the ideal LP (not the CPs)`; `entriesForKind CircularPolarizer returns EXACTLY the two CP presets (not the LP)`; `tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id`; `libraryTrees returns at least one tree and every leaf entry id resolves`; `every seeded sample round-trips store-lookup by its Guid entry id`; `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once`; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds`; `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds`. The first 7 read `(this.liveStores ()).library` where they read the module-level `proxy` (`BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`, step 52), so they prove the live view the composition roots build rather than the fixture's preset double; their assertions are unchanged. `the live Library's By kind tree holds every live entry exactly once` saves its user source and its sample through the record's `sources` and `samples` where it composed `liveLibrary` over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` itself; `the library-entry store derives its By kind tree from what it holds` and `the preset store serves an added preset by kind and by id, and refuses an id it already holds` (step 77) build their store with `emptyPresetStore ()`. `type LibraryProxyTests () = inherit LibraryProxyContract ()` is the in-memory composition: `liveStores` answers `liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources` over a new `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` and a new `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, with those `samples` and `sources`, as `AppContext.create` composes them (step 44), and `emptyPresetStore` is `Library.createInMemory ()`. The facts over no store stay members of `LibraryProxyTests` alone: `ElementId round-trips through its value accessor`; `a MINTED SampleId round-trips create-store-lookup through a proxy of the same shape`; `a STUB proxy of the same shape drives the same kind-constraint logic`; `a Sample entry's fullDescription is exactly its curated description`; `a non-Sample entry's fullDescription is prose built from its kind`; `every seeded entry has a non-empty fullDescription`; `expandedFilms mirrors RepeatBuilder.expand (count copies of the cell, order preserved)`; `forKinds maps each entry case to its valid catalogue kinds`; `the By kind tree groups entries by kind, then facet, then leaf`; `the seeded sample ids are distinct, non-empty Guids`. The module-level `proxy` goes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `LibraryProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id. The abstract contract gets no `ADD_TEST`, and the file keeps its compile position.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `LibraryProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the 10 live-Library and preset-store facts and `LibraryProxyTests` its in-memory subclass; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every LibraryProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.
